Clawpump/claw-agent @ 7b81ee9 (upstream hermes-agent 0.20.6): the MCP trust
tier reads `annotations.readOnlyHint` with getattr(), but mcp>=2.0 renamed the
field to `read_only_hint` (camelCase kept only as a serialization alias), so
every tool on an `untrusted` server is treated as write-capable and asks for
consent — including the reads. One line in tools/mcp_tool.py. Apply with
`patch -p1 < this-file` or `git apply this-file` from the fork checkout.
Fork PR: https://github.com/Clawpump/claw-agent/pull/33 (targets 7b81ee9).

diff --git a/tools/mcp_tool.py b/tools/mcp_tool.py
index 40cb82b63..c96c00fd1 100644
--- a/tools/mcp_tool.py
+++ b/tools/mcp_tool.py
@@ -4640,7 +4640,8 @@ def _annotation_read_only_hint(mcp_tool: Any) -> bool:
     if isinstance(annotations, dict):
         hint = annotations.get("readOnlyHint")
     else:
-        hint = getattr(annotations, "readOnlyHint", None)
+        # mcp >= 2.0 names the SDK field ``read_only_hint``; ``readOnlyHint`` is only its wire alias.
+        hint = mcp_field(annotations, "read_only_hint", "readOnlyHint")
     return hint is True
 
 
